{"dog":{"age_group":"young","application_url":"https://www.nycacc.org/adopt/adoption-process/","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Domestic Short Hair Cross","breed_primary":"Domestic Short Hair Cross","description_text":"My foster writes: Think of Fork as a curious girl who wants to be your friend, who just needs to feel safe first. Right now she is still shy and spends most of her time hiding away, but we often see her popping her head out the door to observe us. At night or when we are not looking, she comes alive doing zoomies, playing with her toys, and watching birds by the window.\nFork will benefit from a quiet and chill adult-only household with someone who has some experience with cats and understands their boundaries. She is very independent, so she would be a great fit for a working household.\n\nAnother foster writes:\nFork is a little, shy gal who is still learning to trust humans. She prefers quiet locations that are enclosed, like a cave-style bed, underneath cabinets, or litter boxes with a top. She will need time getting used to you and your routine but patience will result in a quiet, but loyal companion.","detail_url":"https://nycaccpets.shelterbuddy.com/animal/animalDetails.asp?s=adoption&searchTypeId=4&animalType=2%2C15&pagesize=75&task=view&tpage=6&searchType=4&animalid=198745","id":"53835e8bb4402e02cb7111e6565c03f0","image_urls":["https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/c0c0bc2c018c466c8346b698bdaf510d-1775669070-1775669084-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/1890b89f91c746478a48350d91888ede-1775669071-1775669071-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/4bbfc84e9d0b4d4aa199db7852170333-1775669070-1775669070-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/9983ff6fcf1f4534887fea36fea621b9-1775669070-1775669070-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/088c7f5d6513488bac49ae5ab8ff53a7-1775669070-1775669070-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/